    "body": "OK.  We do need to actually pass the tokenized features to somewhere where CSSOM will see it...\r\n\r\nBut fwiw, on the HTML spec front just removing \"noopener\" from the tokenized features before passing on to the lower layer would presumably fix this problem, in that it would make it clear that noopener has no effect on the appearance....  Then we could at least file bugs on implementations to fix their broken stuff.",
